  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- ***#+Smeagol's Tale**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- ***#@Ramble On**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- ***@^The Wizard**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [6]\n- **@Fire**: back after 147 archived shows (1045 days); rare: 7 archived performances [6]\n- ***@When It's Lamplighting Time In The Valley**: back after 407 archived shows (3058 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [6]\n- **#@^Sorrow Is A Highway**: rare: 12 archived performances [6]\n- **Billy Greets The Crowd**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n- **@Mother's Not Dead, She's Only Sleeping**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [6]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2022-10-31** (recommended): source not stated; 26 songs; 154 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]\n- **billystrings2022-10-31.DPA4018**: source not stated; 25 songs; 156 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Billy [1]\n- The drum set and electric bass visible on arrival signaled to the reviewer that the last Asheville night would be special [4]\n- Gollum appeared playing cello, and Billy invited extra band members onstage; costumes were worn by people at the show [4]\n- The reviewer saw this as their eighth Billy show and third Asheville night; earlier nights were epic, but this one felt legendary [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2022-10-31**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V'S>Lunatec V2>Sound Devices 722 (24/44.1) [1]. Also: Recorded with Schoeps CCM4V mics through Lunatec V2 preamps into a Sound Devices 722 at 24-bit/44.1kHz; Mics placed on-stage-center, barely in front of board, using a 9.5-foot stand; processed in Sound Forge, converted to 16-bit FLAC [1]\n- **billystrings2022-10-31.DPA4018**: taped by John Bell; source: DPA 4018ER 500(DIN)> Sound Devices Mixpre-10 II @32/48 [2]",
